{"kind":"promise","text":"I will implement the docset citation gate on a fresh request/docset-citation-integrity branch, extending the existing real-workroom gate rather than replacing it.\n\nThe classification I will enforce, and the reason each falls where it does. A retired artifact fails: the pointer was withdrawn, so a page citing it names nothing current, and that is unambiguous. An artifact at a path normal succession cannot maintain fails — `.`, comma-joined, absolute filesystem, or branch-name — because no merge will ever publish at that string, so the citation can never flare and its silence reads as currency. A stale but live artifact reports and does not fail, because every artifact at every core package is world-stale today; failing on stale would redden the suite for the whole documentation set, including work you have already reviewed and told me to keep honestly stale.\n\nI will keep the explicit no-workroom skip, and cover it with a test, because a gate that resolves against the durable log cannot run in a fresh clone and must say so rather than pass silently.\n\nI will repair docs/concepts/work-loop.md's three unsupersedable citations to truthful live real-path artifacts, and record a narrow exception with a reason only if the page's actual claim has no maintainable path — I will not invent an anchor to clear a gate I am writing.\n\nFocused tests for every path class, retired versus stale, and the skip. make docs, the relevant Go tests and git diff --check. Exact-head artifacts for internal/docset and docs, then independent review.","body":{"branch":"request/docset-citation-integrity"}}